{"id":"af389c83081b5b62","group":"58","path":"58/batch04/58-df-zfc-forcing10-revised-countable-support.md","title":"ZFC Forcing10 Revised Countable Support","display":"df-zfc-forcing10-revised-countable-support — ZFC Forcing10 Revised Countable Support","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-forcing10-revised-countable-support","aliases":["58-df-zfc-forcing10-revised-countable-support"],"display":"df-zfc-forcing10-revised-countable-support — ZFC Forcing10 Revised Countable Support","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","[[../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-zfc-forcing12-support-iteration-condition.md]]","[[../batch11/58-df-zfc-forcing10-iteration-support.md]]","[[../batch14/58-df-zfc-forcing-relation.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-forcing10-revised-countable-support"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-forcing10-revised-countable-support</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-forcing10-revised-countable-support — ZFC Forcing10 Revised Countable Support"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md\">../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"81cabbac7fa4d75d\" href=\"?note=81cabbac7fa4d75d\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md\">../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"3c61920d957fb9dd\" href=\"?note=3c61920d957fb9dd\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-zfc-forcing12-support-iteration-condition.md\">../batch07/58-df-zfc-forcing12-support-iteration-condition.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"83681d68660fc758\" href=\"?note=83681d68660fc758\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-zfc-forcing10-iteration-support.md\">../batch11/58-df-zfc-forcing10-iteration-support.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"911508dbd8495663\" href=\"?note=911508dbd8495663\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-zfc-forcing-relation.md\">../batch14/58-df-zfc-forcing-relation.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md\">../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,p,\\delta,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\leq_\\bullet,s\\in V\">\\(M,p,\\delta,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\leq_\\bullet,s\\in V\\)</span> (ground model, condition, length, stage posets, iterands, stage orders, and support)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ordinal}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ordinal}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LimitOrdinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{LimitOrdinal}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> are the canonical predicates from the dependencies</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SupportIterationCondition}(p,M,\\delta,\\delta,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet)\">\\(\\operatorname{SupportIterationCondition}(p,M,\\delta,\\delta,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10IterationSupport}_S(s,p,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\delta)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10IterationSupport}_S(s,p,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\delta)\\)</span> bind the iteration condition and its support</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi_{\\mathrm{cf}\\omega}(v_0)\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\in}^{(1)}\">\\(\\varphi_{\\mathrm{cf}\\omega}(v_0)\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\in}^{(1)}\\)</span> is a fixed membership-language formula defining “<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_0\">\\(v_0\\)</span> has cofinality <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega\">\\(\\omega\\)</span>”</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S(M,q,\\varphi,\\vec\\tau,P,\\leq_P)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S(M,q,\\varphi,\\vec\\tau,P,\\leq_P)\\)</span> is the canonical six-argument forcing predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10RevisedCountableSupportData}_S\\subseteq V^7\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10RevisedCountableSupportData}_S\\subseteq V^7\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10RevisedCountableSupport}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10RevisedCountableSupport}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing10\\text{-}revised\\text{-}countable\\text{-}support\\text{-}data}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10RevisedCountableSupportData}_S(M,p,\\delta,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\leq_\\bullet,s)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\delta)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(P_\\bullet,\\delta\\cup\\{\\delta\\},\\operatorname{ran}(P_\\bullet))\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\delta,\\operatorname{ran}(\\dot Q_\\bullet))\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\leq_\\bullet,\\delta\\cup\\{\\delta\\},\\operatorname{ran}(\\leq_\\bullet))\n\\land\\operatorname{SupportIterationCondition}(p,M,\\delta,\\delta,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10IterationSupport}_S(s,p,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\delta)\n\\land|s|\\leq\\aleph_0\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\delta\\cup\\{\\delta\\}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LimitOrdinal}_S(\\alpha)\\land\\sup(s\\cap\\alpha)=\\alpha\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{43mm}\\to\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\!\\left(M,p\\upharpoonright\\alpha,\n\\varphi_{\\mathrm{cf}\\omega},\\langle\\check\\alpha\\rangle,\nP_\\bullet(\\alpha),\\leq_\\bullet(\\alpha)\\right)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing10\\text{-}revised\\text{-}countable\\text{-}support\\text{-}data}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10RevisedCountableSupportData}_S(M,p,\\delta,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\leq_\\bullet,s)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\delta)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(P_\\bullet,\\delta\\cup\\{\\delta\\},\\operatorname{ran}(P_\\bullet))\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\delta,\\operatorname{ran}(\\dot Q_\\bullet))\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\leq_\\bullet,\\delta\\cup\\{\\delta\\},\\operatorname{ran}(\\leq_\\bullet))\n\\land\\operatorname{SupportIterationCondition}(p,M,\\delta,\\delta,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10IterationSupport}_S(s,p,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\delta)\n\\land|s|\\leq\\aleph_0\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\delta\\cup\\{\\delta\\}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LimitOrdinal}_S(\\alpha)\\land\\sup(s\\cap\\alpha)=\\alpha\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{43mm}\\to\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\!\\left(M,p\\upharpoonright\\alpha,\n\\varphi_{\\mathrm{cf}\\omega},\\langle\\check\\alpha\\rangle,\nP_\\bullet(\\alpha),\\leq_\\bullet(\\alpha)\\right)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing10\\text{-}revised\\text{-}countable\\text{-}support}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10RevisedCountableSupport}_S(p,\\delta)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists M,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\leq_\\bullet,s\\in V\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10RevisedCountableSupportData}_S(M,p,\\delta,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\leq_\\bullet,s)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing10\\text{-}revised\\text{-}countable\\text{-}support}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10RevisedCountableSupport}_S(p,\\delta)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists M,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\leq_\\bullet,s\\in V\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10RevisedCountableSupportData}_S(M,p,\\delta,P_\\bullet,\\dot Q_\\bullet,\\leq_\\bullet,s)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The seven-argument predicate is the nondegenerate interface: the ground model, stage posets, iterands, orders, and computed support are explicit.</li>\n<li>The two-argument predicate is retained only as an existential compatibility projection for downstream atoms.</li>\n<li>At an unbounded-support limit, the forcing judgment uses the canonical six-argument relation and a fixed formula code instead of an untyped infix <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Vdash\">\\(\\Vdash\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch01/58-df-limitordinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"81cabbac7fa4d75d","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","locati